\begin{abstract}
This report is generated from completed solver outputs. The generated tables,
sanity checks, and figures are traceable through \texttt{run\_manifest.csv} and
\texttt{figure\_manifest.csv}; no result values are entered by hand.
\end{abstract}
\section{Governing equations and reference quantities}
The solver advances the conservative two-dimensional compressible
Navier--Stokes state
\[
  \mathbf U=[\rho,\rho u,\rho v,\rho E]^T,
  \qquad
  \frac{\partial\mathbf U}{\partial t}+
  \frac{\partial\mathbf F^i}{\partial x}+
  \frac{\partial\mathbf G^i}{\partial y}=
  \frac{\partial\mathbf F^v}{\partial x}+
  \frac{\partial\mathbf G^v}{\partial y}.
\]
The inviscid fluxes are
\[
 \mathbf F^i=[\rho u,\rho u^2+p,\rho uv,u(\rho E+p)]^T,\qquad
 \mathbf G^i=[\rho v,\rho uv,\rho v^2+p,v(\rho E+p)]^T.
\]
The calorically perfect gas closure is
\(p=(\gamma-1)\rho e\), \(E=e+\tfrac12(u^2+v^2)\), and
\(a=\sqrt{\gamma p/\rho}\).  Each case file provides the reference density,
velocity, length, pressure, and force-reference area.  Force coefficients use
\(q_\infty=\tfrac12\rho_\infty U_\infty^2\) and the supplied reference area.
For laminar cases the constant viscosity is evaluated as
\(\mu=\rho_\infty U_\infty L_{Re}/Re\), with
\(k=\mu c_p/Pr\).

\section{Spatial discretization and boundary conditions}
The implementation is a cell-centred finite-volume method on the imported CGNS
unstructured triangles and quadrilaterals.  Face residuals are assembled once
with opposite signs on adjacent owned cells.  Least-squares primitive-variable
gradients support linear face reconstruction, and an active Barth--Jespersen
limiter bounds each reconstructed primitive component by its neighbouring
values.  Density and temperature are floored at reconstructed faces; a
positivity line search rejects nonphysical conservative updates.

Inviscid faces use a local Lax--Friedrichs/Rusanov approximate Riemann flux.
Laminar faces use the reconstructed velocity and temperature gradients to form
the Newtonian stress tensor and Fourier heat flux.  The far field is evaluated
from a characteristic trace.  Slip walls impose zero normal velocity and use
the exact pressure traction; no-slip adiabatic walls impose zero reported wall
velocity, a wall-normal velocity gradient, and zero wall-normal temperature
gradient.  Pressure and tangential viscous forces are accumulated separately,
so the reported skin friction is not contaminated by normal viscous traction.

\section{Implicit iteration and physical-time integration}
Steady cases use local pseudo-time stepping with the case-supplied CFL
continuation schedule.  The frozen residual is corrected by a rank-local
block LU--SGS Euler/Rusanov preconditioner: owned--owned $4\times4$ frozen
Euler/Rusanov couplings are swept locally while inter-rank corrections remain
lagged.  Its diagonal retains the pseudo-time contribution, the flux-consistent
half Rusanov self term, and a viscous safety bound.  A safeguarded matrix-free
Newton line search is available for difficult steady branches; every accepted
candidate is tested against the fully assembled physical residual.  Every
outer residual and force is a global MPI reduction.

The Re~200 cylinder computation uses a BDF1 startup followed by BDF2,
\[
 \frac{A}{2\Delta t}\left(3U^{n+1}-4U^n+U^{n-1}\right)+R(U^{n+1})=0.
\]
For every physical step the two history states remain frozen during the inner
solve.  A second-order extrapolation is used only as the initial nonlinear
guess.  The accepted residual includes both the spatial residual and BDF term;
an attempt that misses the configured reduction target is restored and retried
at a reduced pseudo-CFL without advancing the history or emitting a force row.
The reported inner statistics therefore refer only to accepted physical steps
and explicit failed attempts.

\section{MPI decomposition, output, and reproducibility}
The global cell adjacency graph is partitioned with METIS.  Each rank stores
only owned cells, its one-ring ghosts, and neighbour-scoped send/receive maps.
Halo exchange uses nonblocking neighbour point-to-point communication for
states and gradients; full mesh and full conservative-state replication are
not used during iterations.  Rank-local VTU pieces and a PVTU index preserve
the distributed final field.  The report reader merges only those real pieces
for rendering; it never constructs synthetic field data.

Build with \texttt{cmake -S solver -B solver/build} followed by
\texttt{cmake --build solver/build}, then run
\texttt{mpirun -np <ranks> solver/build/cfd\_solver solve --case <case.json>
--output <directory>}.  The generated manifest records the exact command,
rank count, wall time, and status for every submitted output, and the figure
manifest links every plot below to its source CSV or field file.

