\section{Interpretation and limitations}
The generated residual, force, surface, Mach, and pressure figures are the
evidence for each status in the following section.  At zero angle of attack,
the NACA cases are checked for near-symmetric lift; viscous cases are checked
for zero reported wall speed and nonzero skin friction.  Cylinder cases are
checked for positive mean drag, and the Re~200 case additionally requires
nonzero post-startup lift variation before it can be called statistically
periodic.  The rank-count table is descriptive rather than a claim of ideal
strong scaling: it records only runs actually supplied to the generator.

The method deliberately uses a robust frozen Euler/Rusanov approximate
Jacobian and rank-local block-Jacobi treatment across MPI interfaces.  These
choices favour positivity and reproducibility over the sharper shocks and
faster low-Mach convergence that a fully coupled Roe/HLLC or globally coupled
Krylov implementation could provide.  A case listed under ``Convergence
qualifications'' reached a stationary bounded-residual termination, rather
than the requested residual-reduction target.  Its schema-required
\texttt{converged} status must therefore not be read as a claim that the
target was attained; the generated notes and residual histories make that
limitation explicit.  No case is described as successful if its generated
sanity status is failed.
